      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Issue still present on \nVRCSDK3-2019.12.21.16.01\nUDONSDK-2019.12.22.12.32_Public\n\nalso forgot to include subgraph asset in original post:\nhttps://nyanpa.su/f/vrc/add1.asset\n\nAlso to add on, this issue also seems happen if multiple subgraphs (regardless if the same or not) are used within the same execution path after any node that requires the use of a JUMP instruction, such as Branches, For and While loops. It also affects the JUMP_IF_FALSE instruction used for exiting the for/while loop. \n\nWhen using 2 different subgraphs, only one of subgraph is compiled into the udon assembly. JUMP target addresses however, target an address with the assumption that both subgraphs were in the assembly source. With the same subgraph called twice, the JUMP target address also assumes that the same subgraph is there twice. For example in the test case in my post, the compiled subgraph is 36 bytes long. The target address 0x000053 is offset by 36 bytes from the correct target address of 0x00002F.\n\nEdit: Looks like using different subgraphs regardless of any branching/loops also results in only one of them being compiled into the assembly.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
